      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Pennsylvania Railroad arrived mid‑1800s, making Merion the first rail stop in Lower Merion and sparking suburban growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Merion_Station,_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The SEPTA Paoli/Thorndale Line station, originally built in 1865 and rebuilt in 1917, reflects the Victorian‑era heritage of the Main Line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Merion_Station,_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Merion Civic Association, founded in 1913, later built a community center to honor 81 men who served in World War I.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
